olved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": true, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170413 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/e3471526f4c71b2c4ee00117e125e179da01e6e2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\nThe directory read errored (\"File not found\" \u2014 this read tool doesn't list directories), so I'll use glob to list the files instead.\n[tool: glob]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\nLet me check the factory and search tests for ordering expectations.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\nNow applying fixes.\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: edit]\nAll 16 tests now pass with `python3 -m unittest`. Before, 15 ran and 10 failed; once the broken import in `search.py` was fixed, that module's tests could load too.\n\n**The pre-fix reads:**\n- **(a)** Reading `catalog/` directly failed with \"File not found\". This read tool only reads files, not folders, so I listed the files with glob instead.\n- **(b)** Offset 0, limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135.\n- **(c)** Offset 3, limit 5 returned only lines 4\u20138. Lines 4\u20135 also appeared in (b), so the two ranges overlap.\n\n**Fixes in `catalog/` (tests unchanged):**\n- `books.py:22`: `parse_book` now turns the year into an integer, so `year` equals 1965 and `age()` works.\n- `members.py:4`: the borrow limit was 3 but the comment says five books, so I changed it to 5.\n- `search.py:3`: it i